Z||000003||HugGRRRFiero||09-06-2000||10:29 PM||||I'm not for sure, but I would say Chevettes, Citations, 80's Sunfires, Cavaliers, or Pontiac 6000's might possibly use the same handle.  You know what, I had thought about this question answering a Greg's post earlier today, deja vu.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Maybe someone here knows for sure.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">  <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Linx||09-08-2000||01:38 AM||||Oh yeah- that handle was used everywhere.  As a matter of fact, NAPA carries 'em in bubble packs in their stores.  Very very common.  The Fiero handle...well, on mine anyways, has a raised plastic trim insert in the center of the handle...the NAPA handle doesnt, and differs only in that respect.  No one notices.  If i remember correctly, it was like $21.<P>Come to think of it, Ive seen the same handle in Autozone...but they never had the passenger side. I guess the driver's side is the one that always breaks.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
